   "subject": "Re: Re-name axes from itemplot() in two dimensional MIRT",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You&#39;ve stumbled upon an area where I had to cut some corners to make itemplot() highly general. You still can edit the plot the way you need, because lattice is the system used here and the internals are always exposed. E.g.,<div><br></div><div>```</div><div>mod &lt;- mirt(Science, 2)</div><div>plt &lt;- itemplot(mod, 1)</div><div>print(plt)</div><div>str(plt)</div><div>plt$panel.args.common$xlab &lt;- &#39;my label&#39;</div><div>plt$panel.args.common$ylab &lt;- &#39;my other label&#39;<br></div><div>print(plt)</div><div>```</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers.</div><div><br></div><div>Phil</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Mar 5, 2015 at 5:09 PM, Garett Howardson <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">garett.h...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
